  id: W4_C
  era: Late 18th century
  title: Bronze cannon of Mysore (replica)
  text: Bronze cannon of Mysore (replica). Haidar Ali and his son Tipu Sultan built a modern army with European-style artillery cast in their own foundries. Mysore's forces also used iron-cased war rockets that impressed their British opponents. Many of Tipu's bronze cannons, decorated with tiger-stripe patterns, were captured in 1799 and are displayed today in Britain and India. Captured Mysore rockets were studied in Britain and inspired the Congreve rockets later used in the Napoleonic Wars.
